chlorine wrote:

    [...]
> About the rng, I've noticed after having finally compiled
> nethack myself, that there's a way to define the random
> functions if the correct one are not provided by your system.
> Does this mean that we are not all supervised by the same rng?

Yes.  Nethack doesn't have a random generator of its own, but
depends on one provided by the system.  The standard C library
guarantees one, but the quality of that one often varies, so
Nethack provides a means of using a better one, if it is
available.

Note that even without this option, the standard C generator is
not the same everywhere.

> This is very unsettling...

In some ways, yes.  I'll admit that given the number of high
quality RGN available on the network, I'm a bit surprised that
nethack doesn't just incorporate one of those.

